UPDATE blog_posts SET
  blocks = $blk$[{"id": "451df259-279e-449b-97bf-00f14ae12224", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Every agency will tell you they use AI. Far fewer will tell you when it\u2019s let them down \ud83d\udc40</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">We use AI tools here at Trapeze Media. But we\u2019ve also spent the last 15 years developing the kind of sector-specific, messy human knowledge that no LLM has managed to replicate yet. This is our honest take on where the dividing line sits in mid-2026.</p>"}, {"id": "5b2f0df6-51a8-4e27-be2a-39d080ef5228", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "ai-is-great-at-pattern-recognition-but-has-no-idea-what-s-going-on", "content": "AI is great at pattern recognition (but has no idea what\u2019s going on)"}, {"id": "a357c605-fb5f-4376-b3a2-4eaa31e92c68", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Let\u2019s be real about what AI advertising tools actually do well.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Performance analysis, identifying patterns in large datasets, dynamic creative testing, and smart bidding can all be done quite effectively, at a faster speed and at greater scale than a team of humans doing it manually.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">We use these capabilities every day, and our clients\u2019 campaigns are better for it.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">But, here\u2019s the catch: AI optimises for signals. It doesn\u2019t understand <em>context</em>.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">It doesn\u2019t know that a campaign for a private medical clinic needs completely different language depending on whether someone is in early research mode or ready to book, and that the difference can\u2019t always be read from a click signal.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">It doesn\u2019t understand that a restaurant group running ads during a cost-of-living crunch needs messaging calibrated to <em>feel</em> accessible, not just price-competitive. It can\u2019t read the cultural moment. It won\u2019t tell you when the rules have changed overnight and your entire strategy needs rethinking before 9am.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">You can prompt it to understand these things, plug context into its memory, and so on, but there comes a sort of inflexion point where it\u2019s like, well, at this level of granular hand-holding, I\u2019m probably gonna get it done quicker myself. Especially when models start to trip over themselves with increasing complexity.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">That\u2019s where yours truly comes in, as the people who build the strategy, understand the audience, and know when the tool\u2019s output makes sense and when it\u2019s <strong>confidently, efficiently wrong</strong>.</p>"}, {"id": "37ad0f80-fb60-4be8-9c45-2b1891e45e77", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "the-limitations-we-ve-actually-hit", "content": "The limitations we\u2019ve actually hit"}, {"id": "4abd5a57-c704-4989-8a23-31b86003f497", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">A few things we\u2019ve learned the slightly hard way:</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Tracking is messier than it looks.</strong> AI-powered campaign tools optimise for the signals they can see. If your attribution model has gaps (and most do, as things change fast), you can end up with a system that looks like it\u2019s performing brilliantly while you\u2019re haemorrhaging budget on the wrong audiences.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Relying too much on AI can break your relationship with the data and open fissures in your models, so it\u2019s vital to check in on what the automations are doing.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">We\u2019ve had to go back to basics with clients more than once: check the data, question what\u2019s being measured, and make sure the machine is optimising for something real.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>AI can\u2019t read your website if it\u2019s built in JavaScript.</strong> This one surprised some of our clients. A significant chunk of AI-driven search tools can\u2019t crawl JavaScript-rendered content, which means a beautifully-designed, technically sophisticated website can be effectively invisible to the systems increasingly driving discovery. It\u2019s a straightforward fix once you know about it, but it\u2019s the kind of thing that falls off the radar if no-one\u2019s asking the right questions.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>AI-generated copy has a tell.</strong> We can all clock it now. That slightly over-polished, suspiciously-balanced prose that reads like it was written by someone who has read everything but experienced nothing (you can pry our em-dashes from our cold, dead hands, though).</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">On platforms like TikTok, audiences are particularly brutal about it. We use a bit of AI for drafting and ideation, sure, but not a lick of marketing prose makes it into our campaigns unless it\u2019s been reviewed and rewritten by a human who understands your brand and your audience.</p>"}, {"id": "cc04b6ef-9913-45a2-add7-201b6a848e4f", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "where-ai-has-genuinely-changed-how-we-work", "content": "Where AI has genuinely changed how we work"}, {"id": "e118ca58-6aec-449a-8c9f-bdf30162a432", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">To be fair to the robots, the shift in capability over the past couple of years has been real, and we\u2019d be doing our clients a disservice if we pretended otherwise.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Weather-triggered campaign automation is a good example. We connect live meteorological data to Google Ads and paid social campaigns, so messaging switches automatically based on real-time conditions at your target locations.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">A terrace dining ad when it hits 20\u00b0C near a venue. A comfort food offer when rain comes in. The kind of reactive, hyperlocal advertising that would have taken a team of people monitoring dashboards and manually swapping assets is now running 24/7, automatically, within a strategic framework we\u2019ve built (and which a human team is still overseeing).</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Performance data analysis, too. Identifying which creative variations are working, which audience segments are underperforming, where budget is leaking \u2014 all tasks that used to require an analyst wading through Looker Studio can now surface in near real-time. This is where AI earns its keep.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Our throughline right now is less \u2018can AI do this?\u2019 and more \u2018should AI lead on this, or should a human?\u2019 Just that mindset shift can make you way more impervious to the hyped-up promises of the AI grift machine.</p>"}, {"id": "21965fdc-dd1f-42d0-b4f6-6a79ba8f7bd2", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "chasing-humans-not-platforms", "content": "Chasing humans, not platforms"}, {"id": "8fda1466-3910-4a2a-8947-7bc3526cbf30", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">One thing the past 24 months have made increasingly clear: optimising for platforms is becoming a losing game.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Algorithms change. AI Overviews cannibalise clicks. TikTok\u2019s future in various markets remains a policy discussion as much as a marketing one. The platforms that mattered most three years ago aren\u2019t necessarily the ones that will matter most in three years\u2019 time.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">What doesn\u2019t change is the underlying question: where are the actual humans you want to reach, and what do they need to hear from you in that moment?</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">That\u2019s a question that requires someone who understands your sector, your audience psychology, and the specific context of your brand.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">AI can help you find data and information, but we believe it can\u2019t give you the final answer. LLMs only know what\u2019s out there for them to pillage on the internet. Believe it or not, there\u2019s a whole lot of wisdom knocking around in people\u2019s heads that never makes it to the world wide web.</p>"}, {"id": "e60bb7aa-a779-428c-8895-f633c1678ee7", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "a-few-things-we-re-keeping-firmly-human", "content": "A few things we\u2019re keeping firmly human"}, {"id": "b3fcb823-70d2-415e-9d43-07e06eeb93a8", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Regulatory compliance.</strong> In sectors like private medical and food advertising, the rules are specific, constantly evolving, and consequential if you get them wrong.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">The UK\u2019s \u2018less healthy food\u2019 ad ban is a recent example. A Ministerial statement confirmed that brand advertising not featuring a specific less healthy product is out of scope, but working out what that means for your actual campaign? That requires a human who\u2019s been tracking the legislation and knows how the ASA is interpreting it. As for coming up with smart workarounds to meet compliance? Nothing\u2019s gonna beat a group of creative human minds standing around batting ideas back and forth.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Strategy and creative direction.</strong> Every campaign brief we work on starts with a human being asking: what is this brand actually trying to achieve, who are the specific people we\u2019re trying to reach, and what\u2019s the most compelling way to reach them? AI can generate a lot of creative options quickly, but it\u2019s a bit hit-or-miss with identifying which one respects your brand voice, fits the cultural context, or is actually going to make someone stop scrolling.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Community management and tone.</strong> When a customer complaint lands on your social channels, or a troll shows up in your comments, or a brand needs to respond to a fast-moving news story\u2026 that\u2019s not something to sign over to the bots just yet. No automation handles nuance well enough to be trusted with your brand\u2019s public voice unsupervised. Use it to speed up responses to common questions and maybe generate the first pass at replies to more difficult queries, certainly, but the final word should be human. And that\u2019ll score a brand bonus points, too. Getting through to a human on the modern bot-plagued web is like being offered a cool glass of water after dragging yourself through a desert.</p>"}, {"id": "46697584-3af0-4217-acd7-4747daa5c48a", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "the-honest-conversation-continues", "content": "The honest conversation continues"}, {"id": "e9763805-e608-4adf-88d7-4cf48bae2731", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">We\u2019re hosting an evening in London on <strong>Thursday 11th June</strong> with a small group of marketers, creatives, and business owners who are similarly unconvinced that AI is either the death of their industry or the thing that will fix everything.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">It\u2019s an after-work drinks and panel event at <a href=\"https://www.bloomsyard.com/regentsplace\">Bloomsyard, Regent\u2019s Place</a> \u2014 proper venue, decent wine, pizza, outdoor space. The panel is called <em>\u2018AI Search Optimisation: An Honest Look at How to Show Up\u2019</em>, and the operative word is honest.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">No pitches. No keynotes. Just real practitioners sharing what\u2019s working, what\u2019s not, and what questions they\u2019re still sitting with.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong><a href=\"#\">Grab a spot here \u2192</a></strong></p>"}, {"id": "a3a2bff1-9005-43f9-9b8f-b3d066e536f2", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "anchor": "faq", "content": "FAQ"}, {"id": "2ba918be-136d-4f7f-a575-9e29e11f991b", "type": "text", "content": "<p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>What does a human-first approach to AI actually mean in practice?</strong></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">It means AI handles the tasks it\u2019s genuinely good at \u2014 pattern recognition, data analysis, campaign automation \u2014 while humans lead on strategy, creative direction, compliance, and anything requiring real context or cultural judgement. We use AI to work faster and smarter, not to replace the expertise that comes from years of working in specific sectors.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Can AI tools really get digital marketing wrong?</strong></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">More than most agencies will admit. AI optimises for the signals it can measure, which means gaps in your attribution model, JavaScript-heavy websites, and anything requiring cultural or contextual reading can all slip through undetected. We\u2019ve had to unpick AI-driven \u2018wins\u2019 for clients that turned out to be optimising the wrong thing entirely.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Is AI-generated content a problem for my brand?</strong></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">It can be, particularly on platforms like TikTok where audiences are quick to spot over-polished, personality-free copy. We use AI for early-stage drafting and ideation, but every piece of copy that goes out under a client\u2019s name is reviewed and rewritten by a human. The tell is always there if you don\u2019t.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>How does Trapeze Media use AI in paid advertising campaigns?</strong></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">We use AI for performance analysis, smart bidding, dynamic creative testing, and automation \u2014 including weather-triggered campaigns that switch messaging based on real-time conditions near your venues. The automation runs within a strategic framework built and monitored by our team, not instead of one.</p>"}, {"id": "add830cf-503b-45da-be4f-7726c8453bac", "type": "newsletter", "heading": "", "subheading": ""}]$blk$::jsonb,
  featured_image = $fi$/images/blog/ai-human-strategy-trapeze-media.webp$fi$,
  is_published = false,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'ai-human-strategy-digital-marketing';